      "username": "Powerhound_2000",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/powerhound_2000/{size}/1859_2.png",
      "created_at": "2016-09-18T19:15:56.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>My understanding as an Alpha tester is that the hit due to Friendly Fire is one instance of damage. &nbsp; Jack Handle then stops that one instance of damage from hitting Setback and instead delivers that one hit to each non-hero target. &nbsp;So this is why you get only two hits. &nbsp; Once from his strike and once from trying to hit Setback due to Friendly Fire. &nbsp;</p>",
      "post_number": 2,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:07:29.402Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 0,
